@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamSafaModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Safa Adhisya";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Safa Adhisya</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    A sign language interpreter and part of the Kopi Cinta team who helps
                    create access to communication between the hearing and Deaf communities.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>Sign Language Interpreter</span>
                    <span>Operations Team</span>
                    <span>Deaf Community</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/safa.jpg" alt="Safa Adhisya">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">Her Journey</p>
                <h3>Realizing There Was Still More to Learn</h3>

                <p>
                    Hello everyone! I am Adhis, part of the Kopi Cinta team and a sign language
                    interpreter. My role is to help provide access to information between the
                    hearing and Deaf communities, and vice versa.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Before joining Kopi Cinta, the world of disability, especially the Deaf
                    community, was not something completely new to me. I had been involved in
                    the community and learned directly from them for a long time.
                </p>

                <p>
                    However, when I finally joined Kopi Cinta, I realized that I had never truly
                    known the Deaf world as deeply as I thought. There were still many things I
                    needed to understand, including Deaf culture and the different ways of
                    interacting with the community.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>Her Role</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Sign language interpretation</li>
                    <li>Communication access</li>
                    <li>Operational coordination</li>
                    <li>SOP support with the Deaf team</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Operations</p>
                <h3>Working Closely With the Deaf Team</h3>

                <p>
                    As part of the operational team, Adhis coordinates matters with the Deaf
                    team, especially tasks related to SOP and daily communication.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Along the way, there have been real struggles and obstacles. However, those
                    challenges made her feel more motivated to learn, improve, and understand
                    the community more deeply.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Passion</p>
                <h3>Where Coffee and Deaf Culture Meet</h3>

                <p>
                    Adhis has always had an interest in both the coffee world and the Deaf
                    community. So when these two worlds came together in Kopi Cinta, there was
                    no reason for her to refuse.
                </p>

                <p>
                    For her, Kopi Cinta is more than just a workplace. It is a space where
                    learning, communication, coffee, and inclusivity can grow together.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>Her Reflection</h3>

            <p>
                To Adhis, inclusivity does not belong to only one person, one brand, or one
                community.
            </p>

            <p>
                Inclusivity belongs to all of us. If we truly want to make it happen, each of us
                has to take responsibility and play our part.
            </p>
        </div>

        <br />

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>